<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|article>

<\body>
  <section|Import and export manuscripts>

  Tessera edits TeXmacs trees in the browser. Import a native <verbatim|.tm>
  file or a <verbatim|.tex> file, then use Export to download the native
  document, LaTeX, or PDF.

  <subsection|Try the workflow>

  1. Return to the manuscript library and choose Import a file. Select a
  <verbatim|.tm> or <verbatim|.tex> document from your device.

  2. Open the imported manuscript and make a small change. The editor keeps
  its structured document and renders it in the browser.

  3. Choose Export, then TeXmacs to keep a native editable copy. Choose PDF
  for a shareable proof, or LaTeX for submission and further editing in
  another LaTeX tool.

  4. Open the exported <verbatim|.tex> file again with Import to see the
  supported LaTeX commands converted back into editable TeXmacs structure.

  <subsection|A useful check>

  LaTeX conversion depends on the packages and commands used by a document.
  After importing a complex project, inspect equations, tables, citations,
  and graphics before relying on the converted result. Keep your original
  file and compare the exported PDF before submission.

  <strong|Practice:> export this lesson to PDF and TeXmacs. Add a new
  equation, then export it to LaTeX and inspect how its structure maps to
  standard commands.
</body>
